# Shared across all infra/docker/*.Dockerfile builds. Docker only honors a .dockerignore
# at the root of the build context, and every Dockerfile here is built with the repo root as
# context (`docker build -f infra/docker/<service>.Dockerfile .`) so the build stage can reach
# workspace packages outside the app's own directory — see infra/docker/README.md.
#
# Keep every apps/*/package.json and packages/*/package.json: `bun install --frozen-lockfile`
# resolves the workspace graph from bun.lock against those manifests, even for workspace members
# a given image doesn't build (e.g. apps/mobile). Only their build artifacts and native toolchain
# directories are excluded below.

# VCS / editor / agent tooling
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.serena
graphify-out

# Dependency + build output (reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image; never trusted from host)
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/storybook-static
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Flutter mobile app: not part of any container image built from this directory, and its native
# toolchain directories are large. package.json is kept (workspace graph integrity, see above).
apps/mobile/android
apps/mobile/ios
apps/mobile/lib
apps/mobile/test
apps/mobile/.dart_tool
apps/mobile/.metadata

# Docs, IaC, and CI config: irrelevant to any application image
docs
infra/terraform
.github

# Test/coverage output and local env files — never belongs in a build context
coverage
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
